From 0d89c12af1154f1c86a40956af8329e91b78be61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:27:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: record reviewed Berkeley lifecycle conversion rules

Track twelve explicit call mappings before their consumer. Preserve original categories, levels and message skeletons. Reuse custom typed database_version and error_code from the earlier SQLite conversion, with generic Name for database filenames. The direct Berkeley version-string call removes only the wrapper string allocation. Exact byte and idempotence fixtures pass. Rule data only: no daemon source change or new functional-suite claim.

Coordinator integration provenance (canonical283 to ordered301):
The scripted commands, tool/rule hashes and historical validation receipts above are original-author provenance for the authored parent. They were not rerun on this composed parent and do not claim byte-for-byte regeneration or validation of it.
Application: git am -3 --keep-cr --keep-non-patch of the exact sealed original mailbox; no new conversion rollout.
Original mailbox applied without source-semantic adaptation at the shared insertion boundary; later explicit native removals are preserved separately.
Composed compile/runtime: pending; no suites or benchmarks run during integration.
